```text
BKP01 - 10.20.40.10
```

MinIO port:

```text
9000
```

Restic repository:

```text
s3:http://10.20.40.10:9000/ag3-plains-pastoral-backups
```

## Checking Backup Result

Backup logs are stored in:

```bash
/var/log/nextcloud-backup.log
```

To check the latest backup result:

```bash
sudo tail -n 20 /var/log/nextcloud-backup.log
```

A successful backup shows:

```text
BACKUP_SUCCESS
```

Restic snapshots can also be checked using:

```bash
sudo bash -c '
set -a
source /etc/restic-nextcloud.env
set +a
/usr/local/bin/restic -o s3.connections=1 snapshots
'
```

## MTU Issue

During testing, Restic became very slow when APP01 MTU returned to 1500.

The MTU was changed back to 1400 using:

```bash
sudo ip link set dev enp26s0 mtu 1400
```

After changing the MTU to 1400, the backup completed successfully.
